config FINGERPRINT_FPC_TEE
	tristate "FPC1020 fingerprint sensor (sweet TEE variant)"
	depends on INPUT_FINGERPRINT && OF && GPIOLIB
	depends on !FINGERPRINT_FPC1020
	help
	  Platform driver for the FPC1020 sensor as wired on sweet: it only
	  powers, resets and forwards the IRQ of the sensor; the TEE talks to
	  it over SPI. The GPIOs and the IRQ are requested on demand through
	  sysfs, so it coexists with the FortSense driver on the same pins.

	  It binds "fpc,fpc1020" like FINGERPRINT_FPC1020 (violet), so only
	  one of the two can be enabled.
